            "name": "search_products",
            "title": "PttAVM ürün arama (kartlar)",
            "description": "Display PTT AVM products to the USER as an interactive card grid (visible UI).\n\nThis is the FINAL, USER-FACING display. **Call it AT MOST ONCE per reply, and\nonly with the results you actually want the user to see** (the final query +\nfilters). Every call paints a NEW grid on screen — calling it twice (e.g. a broad\nsearch then a filtered one) leaves BOTH on screen and confuses the user.\n\nDo your exploring/analysis FIRST, without rendering:\n  - ``find_products`` — fetch product data as text (no UI) to inspect/compare.\n  - ``get_search_filters`` — list valid brands/categories/specs for a query.\nThen call ``search_products`` ONCE.\n\n**Pass ONLY the filters the user actually stated. Do not invent them.** If the\nuser just names what they want (\"iphone 16 telefon arıyorum\"), send ``query``\nand NOTHING else — leave ``sort``, ``size``, ``brands``,\n``min_price``/``max_price``, ``category`` and the toggles at their defaults.\nRelevance ranking already puts the best matches first; an unrequested filter\nsilently hides most of the catalog (a guessed brand + price floor can cut 26.000\nresults to 59) and an unrequested ``sort=price_asc`` puts refurbished/low-end\nitems in front of what the user asked for. Only filter when the user said so\n(\"sadece Apple\", \"5000 TL altı\", \"en ucuzdan sırala\") or when they ask you to\nnarrow a result set they have already seen.\n\n``brands``/``merchants``/``category`` values MUST come from\n``get_search_filters`` (the facet ``value`` slug, e.g. ``apple``,\n``elektronik-c-1``) — never the display label and never a guess. A value that\nmatches no facet returns an EMPTY grid with no error. Brand/merchant labels are\nslug-folded for you; ``category`` is not, so copy it verbatim from the facets.\n\nFiltering is server-side — never filter/sort the returned items yourself (they\nare one page of ``total``). Sort: relevance (default) | price_asc | price_desc |\nnewest | best_seller.\n\nReturns JSON ({type:\"products\", total, query, page, items:[...]}) rendered as\ncards (with built-in Önceki/Sonraki pagination). On failure: {type:\"error\", message}.",
